{number: 119}
{title: Great King of Glory}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Great King of glory, [C] come,
And with Thy [G] favor [D7] crown
This [G] temple as Thine [C] own,
This [G] people [D7] as Thine [G] own:
Beneath this [C] roof, O [G] deign to [D7] show
How [G] God can [C] dwell with [G] men be-[D7] [G] low.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Here [G] may Thine ear at-[C] tend
Our [G] humble, [D7] earnest cries,
And [G] grateful praise as-[C] cend,
Like [G] incense, [D7] to the [G] skies:
Here may Thy [C] Word me-[G] lodious [D7] sound,
And [G] spread ce-[C] lestial [G] joys a-[D7] [G] round.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Here [G] may the list'ning [C] throng
Re-[G] ceive Thy [D7] truth with love,
And [G] converts join the [C] song
Of [G] seraph-[D7] im a-[G] bove:
Till all who [C] go from [G] earth a-[D7] way
Shall [G] join the [C] choir in [G] endless [D7] [G] day.
{end_of_verse}
